  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1236 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nUpper level ridging is forecast to dominate the local area \nthroughout the work week while increased moisture continues to be \npulled from the Gulf into South Central Texas. This translates into \nwarm to warmer weather returning with highs in the 80s over most \nlocations on Tuesday to mid 80 to lower 90s by Friday. The local \narea remains rain-free through this period.\n\nBy next weekend, the upper level ridging shifts to the east of the \nlocal area and allows upper level shortwave disturbances to ride \nalong the southwest to northeast flow aloft. This could bring low \nchances for rain across portions of the southern Edwards Plateau and \nRio Grande especially Sunday. The eastern two-thirds of the local \narea to remain dry.",
